@@ -0,0 +1,19 @@
+# Repair phase-native dispatch ownership
+
+User approved worker submission with controller-owned registration/SSH execution.
+Replace the worker's direct database CLI with a project-local request mailbox.
+The existing CommandWorker services requests with its trusted parent claim while
+pumping logs and heartbeats. Native execution retains the existing validation,
+idempotence, fencing, fixed target, accounting and receipts. No additional agent
+or consumer. One asynchronous native call at a time; retain unknown jobs.
+
+Client writes an atomic bounded request and waits for the matching response. It
+never opens the controller DB. Controller owns claim context and rejects altered
+requests. Waiting/cancellation does not reset experiment identity. Worker exit
+must drain the active native call before phase completion.
+
+Implement service/client and protocol wiring; verify behavior on authorized GPU,
+including mailbox retries/errors/parent exit and existing native lineage tests.
+Update reusable guidance/version, build and install runtime/Skill, adopt at a
+quiet boundary, then confirm actual worker-submitted native dispatch and receipt.
+Publish repair and actual observations to the existing SPECTRUM branch.
