 Follow the evidence through repeated B/C/D work. Do not freeze an old convenient
 F/P/A-style plan before examining the closest published implementation.
 
+## B memory and C evidence loop
+
+B builds durable research memory from papers, actual code and read-only community
+discussions. Reuse the project's existing memory/index rather than inventing a
+parallel store. Each entry retains the question, source URL/revision, code entry
+points, model/data/evaluator/settings, observed evidence versus untested claims,
+applicable conditions, unresolved gaps and relevant experiment/result references.
+Community claims remain leads until checked against primary sources/code/results.
+
+Before each of B02, B03 and B04, use this loop within the same sustained worker:
+
+1. State its current question and retrieve the relevant B memory. Assess whether
+   it answers this question under the actual current conditions; reading a memory
+   entry is not itself proof that it applies.
+2. If sufficient, proceed directly. If incomplete, stale or contradictory, use
+   the relevant B methods to search/read papers, inspect implementations or read
+   Xiaohongshu discussions. Update memory with the new evidence and gaps, then
+   return to the same C question. No full B restart or handoff is required.
+3. Derive the hypothesis and competing explanations, design a discriminating
+   experiment using existing benchmark/model/data/evaluation, and run it on the
+   authorized GPU. Record predictions, settings, raw outputs and uncertainty.
+4. Let results choose the next action: adequate evidence answering the question
+   advances to the next milestone; inconclusive evidence triggers a targeted
+   experiment revision or source refresh; a falsified premise triggers problem
+   revision or selection of another question. Record the reason and next action.
+   A negative result can answer a question; do not optimize toward positive results
+   or discard failed trials. Changed hypotheses/protocols get new versions.
+5. Write C's result and updated boundaries back into the shared memory so later
+   B/C/D reasoning starts from accumulated evidence rather than repeated searching.
+
+B02 retrieves mechanism/assumption evidence; B03 retrieves strong implementations,
+fair comparison settings and reproduction pitfalls; B04 retrieves the combined
+mathematical and experimental evidence to define the problem and its falsifiers.
+These milestones do not launch separate agents. This loop does not waive B05
+independent acceptance, D verification or formal E. Material revisions to already
+accepted evidence still use the typed revisit route.
+
 ## Real GPU execution inside the worker
 
 The CommandWorker injects `response_protocol.phase_native` only after a real
 controller claim. Its context binds project/run/owner/fence to the current live
-phase worker. Invoke the supplied `phase-native --context ... --request ...`
+phase worker. Invoke the exact supplied `phase_mailbox --mailbox ... --request ...`
 command with one request containing `request_id`, `task`, `decision_ref`, and
-`coverage_ref`. The task is native_harness/native, never another general agent.
+`coverage_ref`. The worker submits in its project directory and waits for the
+matching result. The existing dispatcher owns database writes and native SSH
+execution; the worker must not open the runtime database, request broader sandbox
+access or copy the database. The task is native_harness/native, never another general agent.
 Synchronize pinned input/code files to the already fixed target; the existing
 NativeBridge verifies pins and performs actual execution and output collection.
 Do not fabricate future run IDs or receipts to satisfy an input schema.
@@ -70,6 +110,15 @@ unknown jobs retain that slot and must be reconciled under their original identi
 A repeated identical request observes the same child; changed content with the
 same request ID is rejected. The parent cannot complete with unresolved children.
 
+The dispatcher pumps worker logs and heartbeats while serving one native request.
+On dispatcher loss, keep the submitted request and original execution identity;
+resume through reconciliation. Do not turn a repeated infrastructure error into
+new research rounds or claim experimental progress from a live model process.
+Status reports distinguish worker activity, native dispatch, actual GPU execution,
+collected results and scientific acceptance. Installation qualification must include
+a real worker-to-dispatcher call under the deployed worker permissions and a native
+receipt; unit tests or an unsandboxed controller call alone cannot establish this.
+
 Every subsequent request extends the latest worker-local decision and coverage;
 the final phase result extends them again and consumes all actual native receipts,
 including failures. Pending scoring and formal E obligations cannot disappear.
